## 5. Data

```yaml id=DATA kind=data
entities:
  - id: ENT-User
    name: User
    plain_name: Customers
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: phone}
      - {name: email, required: false}
      - {name: avatar, type: image, required: false}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
    seed_guidance: Two sample customers and one store manager with realistic Indian-or-international names
      matching the app locale.
  - id: ENT-Address
    name: Address
    plain_name: Delivery addresses
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: label, description: 'Home, Work, ...'}
      - {name: recipient_name}
      - {name: phone}
      - {name: line1}
      - {name: line2, required: false}
      - {name: city}
      - {name: region, required: false}
      - {name: postal_code}
      - {name: is_default, type: bool}
  - id: ENT-Category
    name: Category
    plain_name: Categories
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: image, type: image, required: false}
      - {name: parent, type: ref, required: false, ref: ENT-Category}
    seed_guidance: Four to six top-level categories that fit the shop (for example clothing, home, electronics).
  - id: ENT-Product
    name: Product
    plain_name: Products
    fields:
      - name: name
      - name: description
        type: text
      - name: price
        type: money
      - name: compare_at_price
        type: money
        required: false
        description: Original price when on sale
      - name: image
        type: image
      - name: gallery
        type: json
        required: false
        description: List of extra image URLs
      - name: category
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-Category
      - name: brand
        required: false
      - name: rating
        type: number
        required: false
      - name: rating_count
        type: int
        required: false
      - name: in_stock
        type: bool
    seed_guidance: 20 to 40 products across the categories with believable names, prices, photos and a
      mix of in-stock and out-of-stock items.
  - id: ENT-ProductVariant
    name: Product variant
    plain_name: Sizes and colors
    fields:
      - name: product
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-Product
      - name: label
        description: For example M / Blue
      - name: sku
      - name: price
        type: money
        required: false
        description: Only when it differs from the product price
      - name: in_stock
        type: bool
  - id: ENT-Cart
    name: Cart
    plain_name: Cart
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: item_count, type: int}
      - {name: subtotal, type: money}
      - {name: shipping_fee, type: money}
      - {name: total, type: money}
  - id: ENT-CartItem
    name: Cart item
    plain_name: Cart items
    fields:
      - {name: cart, type: ref, ref: ENT-Cart}
      - {name: product, type: ref, ref: ENT-Product}
      - {name: variant, type: ref, required: false, ref: ENT-ProductVariant}
      - {name: quantity, type: int}
      - {name: unit_price, type: money}
  - id: ENT-Order
    name: Order
    plain_name: Orders
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: OrderStatus}
      - {name: shipping_address, type: text, description: Address as it was at checkout}
      - {name: items_total, type: money}
      - {name: shipping_fee, type: money}
      - {name: total, type: money}
      - {name: payment_method, type: enum, required: false, enum: PaymentMethodType}
      - {name: placed_at, type: datetime}
      - {name: estimated_delivery, type: date, required: false}
      - {name: tracking_code, required: false}
      - {name: cancel_reason, required: false}
    state_machine:
      field: status
      states: [placed, confirmed, shipped, delivered, cancelled]
      transitions:
        - {from: placed, target: confirmed, 'on': confirm}
        - {from: confirmed, target: shipped, 'on': ship}
        - {from: shipped, target: delivered, 'on': deliver}
        - {from: placed, target: cancelled, 'on': cancel}
        - {from: confirmed, target: cancelled, 'on': cancel}
    seed_guidance: Three sample orders for the main customer, one in each of placed, shipped and delivered.
  - id: ENT-OrderItem
    name: Order item
    plain_name: Items in an order
    fields:
      - {name: order, type: ref, ref: ENT-Order}
      - {name: product, type: ref, ref: ENT-Product}
      - {name: variant, type: ref, required: false, ref: ENT-ProductVariant}
      - {name: name, description: Product name at the time of purchase}
      - {name: quantity, type: int}
      - {name: unit_price, type: money}
  - id: ENT-OrderEvent
    name: Order event
    plain_name: Order progress steps
    fields:
      - {name: order, type: ref, ref: ENT-Order}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: OrderStatus}
      - {name: note, required: false}
      - {name: at, type: datetime}
  - id: ENT-PaymentMethod
    name: Payment method
    plain_name: Saved payment methods
    fields:
      - name: user
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-User
      - name: kind
        type: enum
        enum: PaymentMethodType
      - name: label
        description: Display text only, for example Card ending 4242. Never a full number.
      - name: is_default
        type: bool
  - id: ENT-Payment
    name: Payment
    plain_name: Payments
    fields:
      - {name: order, type: ref, ref: ENT-Order}
      - {name: method, type: enum, enum: PaymentMethodType}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: PaymentStatus}
      - {name: amount, type: money}
      - {name: provider_reference, required: false}
    state_machine:
      field: status
      states: [pending, paid, failed, refunded]
      transitions:
        - {from: pending, target: paid, 'on': capture}
        - {from: pending, target: failed, 'on': decline}
        - {from: paid, target: refunded, 'on': refund}
  - id: ENT-Review
    name: Review
    plain_name: Reviews
    fields:
      - {name: product, type: ref, ref: ENT-Product}
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: rating, type: int, description: 1 to 5}
      - {name: title, required: false}
      - {name: body, type: text, required: false}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
    source: research
  - id: ENT-Favorite
    name: Favorite
    plain_name: Favorites
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: product, type: ref, ref: ENT-Product}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
    source: research
  - id: ENT-Notification
    name: Notification
    plain_name: Notifications
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: kind, type: enum, enum: NotificationKind}
      - {name: title}
      - {name: body, type: text}
      - {name: is_read, type: bool}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
enums:
  - {name: OrderStatus, values: [placed, confirmed, shipped, delivered, cancelled]}
  - {name: PaymentMethodType, values: [card, wallet, bank_transfer, cash_on_delivery]}
  - {name: PaymentStatus, values: [pending, paid, failed, refunded]}
  - {name: NotificationKind, values: [order_update, offer, account]}
seed_guidance: Generate sample records that read like a real business, in the language of the app.
```

## 6. API

```yaml id=API kind=api
operations:
  - id: API-requestOtp
    name: Request sign-in code
    method: POST
    path: /auth/otp
    request_entity: ENT-User
    notes: Sends a one-time code to the phone number. Mock sender in the preview.
  - id: API-verifyOtp
    name: Verify sign-in code
    method: POST
    path: /auth/otp/verify
    request_entity: ENT-User
    response_entity: ENT-User
    notes: Returns the session. New phone numbers create a user.
  - id: API-getMe
    name: Get my profile
    method: GET
    path: /me
    response_entity: ENT-User
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-updateMe
    name: Update my profile
    method: PATCH
    path: /me
    request_entity: ENT-User
    response_entity: ENT-User
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listAddresses
    name: List my addresses
    method: GET
    path: /addresses
    response_entity: ENT-Address
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-createAddress
    name: Add an address
    method: POST
    path: /addresses
    request_entity: ENT-Address
    response_entity: ENT-Address
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-updateAddress
    name: Change an address
    method: PUT
    path: /addresses/{id}
    request_entity: ENT-Address
    response_entity: ENT-Address
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-deleteAddress
    name: Delete an address
    method: DELETE
    path: /addresses/{id}
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listCategories
    name: List categories
    method: GET
    path: /categories
    response_entity: ENT-Category
    response_many: true
  - id: API-listProducts
    name: List products
    method: GET
    path: /products
    response_entity: ENT-Product
    response_many: true
    notes: 'Query: category, sort, filters, page.'
  - id: API-getProduct
    name: Get a product
    method: GET
    path: /products/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Product
    notes: Includes its variants (ENT-ProductVariant).
  - id: API-searchProducts
    name: Search products
    method: GET
    path: /search
    response_entity: ENT-Product
    response_many: true
    notes: 'Query: q, filters, sort, page.'
  - id: API-getCart
    name: Get my cart
    method: GET
    path: /cart
    response_entity: ENT-Cart
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Includes its items (ENT-CartItem).
  - id: API-addCartItem
    name: Add to cart
    method: POST
    path: /cart/items
    request_entity: ENT-CartItem
    response_entity: ENT-Cart
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-updateCartItem
    name: Change cart quantity
    method: PATCH
    path: /cart/items/{id}
    request_entity: ENT-CartItem
    response_entity: ENT-Cart
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-removeCartItem
    name: Remove from cart
    method: DELETE
    path: /cart/items/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Cart
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-createOrder
    name: Place an order
    method: POST
    path: /orders
    request_entity: ENT-Order
    response_entity: ENT-Order
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Turns the cart into an order and empties the cart.
  - id: API-listOrders
    name: List my orders
    method: GET
    path: /orders
    response_entity: ENT-Order
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-getOrder
    name: Get an order
    method: GET
    path: /orders/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Order
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Includes its items (ENT-OrderItem).
  - id: API-getOrderTracking
    name: Get order progress
    method: GET
    path: /orders/{id}/tracking
    response_entity: ENT-OrderEvent
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-cancelOrder
    name: Cancel an order
    method: POST
    path: /orders/{id}/cancel
    response_entity: ENT-Order
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listPaymentMethods
    name: List saved payment methods
    method: GET
    path: /payment-methods
    response_entity: ENT-PaymentMethod
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-addPaymentMethod
    name: Save a payment method
    method: POST
    path: /payment-methods
    request_entity: ENT-PaymentMethod
    response_entity: ENT-PaymentMethod
    auth: authenticated
    notes: The provider tokenizes the card; only the display label is stored.
  - id: API-removePaymentMethod
    name: Remove a payment method
    method: DELETE
    path: /payment-methods/{id}
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-createPayment
    name: Pay for an order
    method: POST
    path: /payments
    request_entity: ENT-Payment
    response_entity: ENT-Payment
    auth: authenticated
    notes: 'Mock provider by default: approves unless the test card for decline is used.'
  - id: API-listReviews
    name: List product reviews
    method: GET
    path: /products/{id}/reviews
    response_entity: ENT-Review
    response_many: true
    source: research
  - id: API-createReview
    name: Write a review
    method: POST
    path: /products/{id}/reviews
    request_entity: ENT-Review
    response_entity: ENT-Review
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-listFavorites
    name: List my favorites
    method: GET
    path: /favorites
    response_entity: ENT-Favorite
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-addFavorite
    name: Save a favorite
    method: POST
    path: /favorites
    request_entity: ENT-Favorite
    response_entity: ENT-Favorite
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-removeFavorite
    name: Remove a favorite
    method: DELETE
    path: /favorites/{id}
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-listNotifications
    name: List my notifications
    method: GET
    path: /notifications
    response_entity: ENT-Notification
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-markNotificationRead
    name: Mark a notification read
    method: POST
    path: /notifications/{id}/read
    response_entity: ENT-Notification
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-registerPushToken
    name: Register this phone for push
    method: POST
    path: /devices/push-token
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Body carries the device token. Mock in the preview.
mock_guidance: A generated mock backend answers every operation; nothing leaves the device in the preview.
```

## 7. Roles

```yaml id=ROLES kind=roles
roles:
  - {id: ROLE-customer, name: Customer, description: 'Shops, pays and tracks orders.'}
```

## 8. Integrations

```yaml id=INTEGRATIONS kind=integrations
items:
  - id: INT-sms_otp
    name: Sign-in codes by SMS
    purpose: Send one-time codes so people can sign in with a phone number.
    notes: Mock sender prints the code in the preview. A real SMS provider is chosen at release.
  - id: INT-order_emails
    name: Order emails
    purpose: Email an order confirmation and shipping updates.
  - id: INT-payments
    name: Payments
    purpose: Take card and wallet payments through a payment provider.
    notes: Mock provider by default. A real provider SDK needs a development build and keeps card data
      off our servers. Online payment only.
  - id: INT-push_notifications
    name: Push notifications
    purpose: Send order updates and offers to the phone.
    notes: Shown as in-app banners in the preview.
  - id: INT-plan_for_a_development_build
    name: Plan for a development build
    purpose: Services with native code need an Expo development build instead of the stock preview client.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-005
  - id: INT-send_codes_and_reminders_from_the_server
    name: Send codes and reminders from the server
    purpose: Text messages and reminders are sent through a provider API from a server, not from the app.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-006
```

## 9. Behavior

```yaml id=BEHAVIOR kind=behavior
offline: Basic cache. The last loaded lists and details stay readable without a connection, and changes
  wait on the phone until the connection returns.
deep_links:
  - /category/[id]
  - /orders/[id]
  - /orders/[id]/tracking
  - /product/[id]
  - /product/[id]/review/new
  - /product/[id]/reviews
notifications: [order update notifications, offer notifications, account notifications]
permission_prompts: ['Notifications, asked after the first useful moment and not at launch']
error_conventions:
  - Show a plain-language message and a retry action, never a raw error code
  - Keep what the person typed when a request fails
  - Loading, empty, error and offline states come from the screen recipe
  - 'Never log personal data (data classification: internal)'
accessibility:
  - Every control has a text label for screen readers
  - Text meets WCAG AA contrast in light and dark mode
  - Text grows with the phone's font size setting
  - Touch targets are at least 44 by 44 points
```

## 10. Screens

### SCR-001 - /welcome

```yaml id=SCR-001 kind=screen
route: /welcome
recipe: welcome
purpose: Introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign in, create an account or just look
  around
flow: FLW-002
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - sign_in: {go: SCR-002}
  - create_account: {go: SCR-003}
  - browse_as_guest: {go: SCR-004}
copy:
  cta_guest: Just looking
  cta_primary: Sign in
  cta_secondary: Create account
  intro: Introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign in, create an account or just look
  title: Shop what you love
checks:
  - Just looking opens the home screen without asking for an account
  - Sign in and Create account open the matching screens
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign
    in, create an account or just look around'
```

### SCR-002 - /login

```yaml id=SCR-002 kind=screen
route: /login
recipe: login-otp
purpose: Sign in with a phone number and a one-time code
flow: FLW-002
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - send_code: {calls: API-requestOtp, on_success: show the code field and start the resend timer}
  - verify_code: {calls: API-verifyOtp, go: SCR-004, on_success: save the session and open the home screen}
  - new_user_setup: {go: SCR-003, on_success: opened instead of home when the number is new}
states:
  wrong_code: {allow: 'retry, and resend after 30 seconds', show: inline error under the code field}
copy:
  cta: Send code
  hint: We will text you a 6-digit code
  intro: Sign in with a phone number and a one-time code
  title: Sign in
checks:
  - A wrong code shows an error and allows another try
  - The resend link stays disabled for 30 seconds after a send
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: sign in with a phone number and a one-time code'
```

### SCR-003 - /signup

```yaml id=SCR-003 kind=screen
route: /signup
recipe: signup
purpose: Finish a new account with a name and an optional email after the phone number is verified
